Performance summary: mean of every metric over case sets
==============================================================================

Source: experiment_result/**/placement_results.json, one selected
layout per case (the records behind overall_table.txt).

Conventions
  * A mean is the arithmetic mean of the per-case values.
  * A method is averaged only over the cases where it has a
    value; n is printed per column, and a cell marked * covers
    fewer cases than the set (footnote below the table).
  * Decimals: BA/WL/Interposer/MaxT/AvgT 2, AR/SAR 3; the stored
    per-case values are averaged, rounding half-up on output.

  all set (n=8): every case the four sweeps cover
  BT  set (n=7): cases bt_tree solves (hp11_m unsolved)
  RLP set (n=4): cases RLP solves (hp11_m, hp8_m, syn1, syn5 unsolved)

